+---
+plan_id: bug-002
+kind: bug
+title: What main still holds after #121 (inv-009)
+created: 2026-10-23
+dag: bug-002.dag.yaml
+parent: inv-009
+---
+# bug-002: What main still holds after #121 (inv-009)
+## Why
+inv-009 answered yes: main @ 6b6bdb5 still holds unfinished and defective work. David accepted all 18 of its
+recommendations and asked for one plan to fix them. Six nodes, one per symptom group; every accepted recommendation
+is closed by exactly one node. Evidence was taken on main @ b8e33bb / 6b6bdb5 on 2026-10-23. Rows are in
+`docs/requirements.md` (SELL-4) and `docs/ui-requirements.md` (the rest).
+
+### N1: A fresh clone F5s straight into Docket
+- Symptom: on a fresh clone, F5 with the API and web profile fails with "Cannot find module …vite/bin/vite.js".
+  With packages restored, the port refuses connections for the whole trail compile. Under `vite preview`, a
+  failed compile is silent. Expected: F5 restores packages or names the command, and the port answers while the
+  compile runs. A failed compile is reported and served as 503 under preview too.
+- Evidence (2026-10-23):
+  - `git grep -n -A2 Docket.Web.esproj Uinsure.Policies.slnx` → `<Build Project="false" />` (:49)
+  - `git grep -n -i "npm\|restore" src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/Docket.Web.esproj` → nothing
+  - `launch.json:9` runs `node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js` directly
+  - the dev server answered after about 60 s in this session (inv-009 recorded 92–128 s on David's machine), because `vite.config.ts:31-42` compiles in the config hook
+  - `apply: 'serve'` (:36) compiles under preview too, and its report lives only in `configureServer` (:51)
+  - `package.json` has no `engines`, and there's no `.nvmrc`
+- Breaks DATA-1 (the trail is compiled and served honestly) and U10's one-key F5 acceptance (`ui.dag.yaml:591`, `:594`).
+- Closes inv-009 #1 and #12.
+
+### N2: The workbench shows the request it sent and the response it got
+- Symptom:
+  - Sell and Cancel render "the request as sent (inspector)" as not built yet.
+  - On claim and renew, the requests drawer starts closed after every send.
+  - On `#/workbench/policies/TEST-0006/claims/new` the drawer rides over the last section mid-page.
+  - Bodies show as one flat line.
+
+  Expected: every workbench screen shows the request it sent and the response it got after a send, laid out in a
+  drawer that never covers content, with JSON indented.
+- Evidence (2026-10-23):
+  - the not-built placeholders: `git grep -n NotBuiltRegion` → `SellPolicy.tsx:406` and `CancelPolicy.tsx:318`
+  - the drawer starts closed: `RequestsDrawer.tsx:28` `useState(false)`
+  - the drawer is mounted inside the last section: `RecordClaim.tsx:253` (Renew mounts it at form level, `RenewPolicy.tsx:232`)
+  - the flat line: `api.ts:286`, `:389`, `:414` use `JSON.stringify(body)` with no indent, and `InspectorDrawer.module.css:154` sets `white-space: pre`
+- Breaks WB-7, and W3's acceptance "an overlay that never covers content" (`ui.dag.yaml:380`).
+- Closes inv-009 #2, #5, #6 and #7.
+
+### N3: The workbench says what the API answered
+- Symptom:
+  - Before and after every sale, the Sell header's Status reads "not in this screen's data".
+  - On a successful sale nothing changes at the Send button.
+  - On Cancel, a failed re-read after a 201 leaves the pre-cancel status unmarked, and a rung receipt can read "answered ,".
+
+  Expected: Status shows the status the API returned. A sale's outcome reaches the user where they are. A status
+  read before the cancel is marked as such, and a missing value is drawn as not returned.
+- Evidence (2026-10-23):
+  - `SellPolicy.tsx:231-239` passes no `status` to `PageHeader`, whose default `missingLabel` is "not in this screen's data" (`PageHeader.tsx:73`)
+  - only error outcomes pass a `focusKey` (`SellPolicy.tsx:250`, `:259`)
+  - `CancelPolicy.tsx:106-109` re-reads and sets the policy only on ok
+  - `:166` and `:195` print `''` when the step isn't done
+- Breaks WB-1, BUSY-1 and HONEST-1.
+- Closes inv-009 #3, #4 and #18. David ruled #4: focus moves to the answer; there is no redirect to the policy view.
+
+### N4: The explorer has no region still marked not built yet
+- Symptom:
+  - Matrix Step 3 shows "Test counts are per node — not built yet".
+  - The AGENT-2 e2e test is `test.fixme`, because the undrawn-lines notice is the screen's own markup.
+  - The Plan nav entry always opens the build plan.
+
+  Expected: the scope note is drawn from `trace.json`'s per-node test counts, the notice is a kit component with the test green, and the Plan nav offers every plan.
+- Evidence (2026-10-23):
+  - `Matrix.tsx:140-147` renders `<NotBuiltYet kind="region" name="test-count scope note" />`
+  - `git grep -n test.fixme tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/e2e/U10/agent-2.spec.ts` → line 23
+  - `Frame.tsx:18` hard-wires `#/plans/${buildPlanId}`, and `:126` picks the first `build` plan
+- Breaks DATA-4, AGENT-2 and DAG-1.
