+<article class="kit-finding-card__card" aria-labelledby="fc-a1-i1" data-testable="true" data-fixed="true" data-comp="finding-card · project · testable"><h3 id="fc-a1-i1" class="kit-finding-card__title"><span class="kit-finding-card__id">I1</span><span class="kit-status-tag__tag kit-status-tag__pass" data-status="pass"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check kit-status-tag__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg><span>Fixed</span></span><span class="kit-finding-card__testable"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-flask-conical kit-finding-card__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2"></path><path d="M6.453 15h11.094"></path><path d="M8.5 2h7"></path></svg><span>Testable</span></span></h3><dl class="kit-finding-card__fields"><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Symptom</dt><dd>live POST /policies/{ref}/claims returns 500 with an InvalidOperationException saying RecordClaimRequest has validation metadata on record property 'Description' that will be ignored.</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Cause</dt><dd>CancellationContracts.cs:38-40 declares RecordClaimRequest as a positional record and targets its DataAnnotations at the generated properties ('[property: Required] DateOnly? ClaimDate' at :39 and '[property: MaxLength(500)] string? Description' at :40). MVC builds a positional record through its primary constructor, so it reads validation metadata from the constructor parameters. When it finds validators on a property that maps to a constructor parameter, it throws during object-model validation instead of quietly ignoring them. The throw happens on every request whose body deserialises into a RecordClaimRequest (PoliciesController.cs:63 binds it from the body), so the happy path, 404, 422 and DataAnnotations-400 cases all become 500s. The stub's canned body at :65 never runs. The exception names only 'Description', but ClaimDate at :39 has exactly the same pattern and is the same cause (not a separate finding). Fixing only :40 would probably just move the exception to ClaimDate; the code doesn't show why MVC reported Description first. COULD-2 says 'claimDate required, description optional, max 500', and the architecture contract says required DTO members are 'nullable and [Required]'. Both constraints have to be enforced as a 400, not dropped or turned into a 500.</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Files</dt><dd><a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/CancellationContracts.cs" aria-label="src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/CancellationContracts.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/CancellationContracts.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a> <a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Controllers/PoliciesController.cs" aria-label="src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Controllers/PoliciesController.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Controllers/PoliciesController.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a></dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Fix direction</dt><dd>put the Required and MaxLength(500) constraints where MVC reads them for this type. Either attach them to the record's constructor parameters, or make the contract a class with settable properties, like the existing SellPolicyRequest (SellPolicyRequest.cs:20, a class whose [Required]/[MaxLength] attributes are on properties). Keep both members nullable. Other F3 request contracts checked, not affected: CancelPolicyRequest (CancellationContracts.cs:6) is a positional record with no validation attributes, so nothing triggers the check, and the gate saw cancel answer 201 live. The quote has no request record: its only constraint is '[FromQuery, Required]' on the action parameter at PoliciesController.cs:51, and action parameters are not subject to this check, so the gate saw quote answer 200 live. The response records (CancellationContracts.cs:8-36, 43-48) carry no DataAnnotations and are never model-validated.</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Suggested test</dt><dd><span class="kit-finding-card__absent">not recorded in the excerpt</span></dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Fixed by</dt><dd><span class="kit-finding-card__fix"><span class="kit-sha-link__wrap" data-state="pop"><a class="kit-sha-link__sha kit-sha-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/commit/9ec61af" aria-label="Commit 9ec61af on GitHub">9ec61af<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-sha-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a></span><span class="kit-finding-card__trailer">trailer text not in the excerpt</span><span>commit subject not in the excerpt</span></span></dd></div></dl></article>
