+# inv-010: N1's listen-first server meets a shell that reads trace.json once
+## Question
+Why does bug-002/N1 FAIL review at attempt 2 (R1: F5 lands on "trace.json could not be read (HTTP 503)" while the trail compiles), and is the cause in the listen-first design, in the shell's one-shot trace load, or in tests that never open the page during the compile?
+## Hypothesis
+Listen-first (35122e4b) moved "ready" from port-bind to compile-end, but Vite's --open fires on listen, not on printUrls, and the shell loads trace.json once and treats a 503 as terminal; no test drives a page against the dev server during the compile. Disproved if Vite opens only after printUrls, if the shell already retries a 503 "compiling", or if a test opens the page mid-compile.
+## Evidence
+- docs/trace/bug-002/N1/verdicts/A2-reviewer.json: FAIL, R1 P1 (F5 lands on the 503 error), R2-R5 P2
+- docs/trace/bug-002/N1/verdicts/A2-security.json: PASS, S1 P2 (dev middleware 500s)
+- docs/trace/bug-002/N1/findings/A2.md: the investigator's diagnosis, I1-I7
+- docs/trace/bug-002/N1/findings/A1.md: attempt 1's gate flake (a different cause, fixed in 9972c248)
+- docs/trace/bug-002/N1/packet/: the reviewed diff, trailers and gates at 9271325
+- `dotnet test --project tests/Uinsure.Policies.Architecture.Tests` at f0423f1, run by the orchestrator: exit 2, LaunchProfileTests expects `node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js`, gets `scripts/dev.mjs` (I7)
+## Findings
+**Yes, all three, with one cause and one trigger.** The cause is the shell's one-shot load: the only reader of /trace.json treats every non-2xx answer as final and asks once. Listen-first's open-on-listen is the trigger, and no test opens a page during the compile. Seven findings, all new; none shares a fingerprint with A1. Details in [findings/A2.md](../../trace/bug-002/N1/findings/A2.md).
+- I1 (new, DATA-1, blocking): `app/data/trace.ts:245-265` turns the compiling 503 into a final error, and `app/shell/Frame.tsx:41-53` never asks again. Vite opens the browser inside listen() (`vite.config.ts:49-50` holds back only the "Local:" line), and an open tab reloads on reconnect. Every path that loads the page mid-compile hits it.
+- I2 (new, DATA-1): `Docket.Web.esproj:4` StartupCommand `npx vite` bypasses the `scripts/dev.mjs` guard. The shipped "API and web" F5 runs the DebugTarget, not this (`Uinsure.Policies.slnLaunch:11-13`, `LaunchProfileTests.cs:69-71`), but it is still a launch path the plan names.
+- I3 (new, DATA-1): `vite.config.ts:53` decodes every request URL before the /trace filter, so a malformed escape on any path is a 500.
+- I4 (new, API8:2023): `vite.config.ts:56-58` accepts a directory, so GET /trace/ throws EISDIR and answers 500.
+- I5 (new, DATA-1): `data-1-first-run.test.ts:218` matches /compil/i, which both 503 bodies satisfy. The two states differ only in prose, which I1's fix must not key on.
+- I6 (new, DATA-1, prose): `data-1-trace-on-start.test.ts:2-5, :147` still describe compile-first.
+- I7 (new, DATA-1, blocking): `LaunchProfileTests.cs:85` still pins the old program, so the .NET suite fails at HEAD and pre-push would refuse the branch. The gates ran npm only.
+## Recommendations
+```yaml recommendations
+- {kind: amend-node, target: bug-002/N1, rule: DATA-1, reason: "I1+I5: web-tester red first: a loader unit test where trace.json answers the compiling state twice then the fixture (ready after 3 requests), guards that the did-not-compile 503 and the 404 stay final after one request, and the toolchain test's first answer pinned to 503 plus the exact compiling marker. Then web-builder: the server marks compiling distinguishably (not prose), and the loader re-asks while it says compiling, keeping DataNotice's existing loading state. No browser-open override (direction b)", status: proposed}
+- {kind: amend-node, target: bug-002/N1, rule: DATA-1, reason: "I7: tester moves LaunchProfileTests' program pin to the guarded entry scripts/dev.mjs (an intended change, shown at Pause 2). The node's gates add dotnet build and the full dotnet test, because it changes files the .NET tests read", status: proposed}
+- {kind: amend-node, target: bug-002/N1, rule: DATA-1, reason: "I2: red test that runs the esproj StartupCommand as written on a copy with no node_modules and expects npm ci named; then the StartupCommand goes through scripts/dev.mjs, keeping --port 4170 --strictPort for DevServerPort", status: proposed}
+- {kind: amend-node, target: bug-002/N1, rule: DATA-1, reason: "I3+I4+I6: in-node, because I1 rewrites the same middleware lines: red tests for GET /src/%E0%A4%A (left to Vite), /trace/%E0%A4%A (4xx) and /trace/ (404); decode only /trace paths and serve regular files only; the tester re-states the stale describe title and header with assertions unchanged", status: proposed}
+```
+## Why
+bug-002/N1's attempt-2 review FAILed on R1 (P1), which made attempt 3, the retry ladder's stop. David is away under a standing delegation ("work autonomously and proceed with your recommendations if you have questions decisions", 2026-10-23), so the recommendations are decided under it.
+## Approach
+Read-only: the A2 verdicts and packet, A1's findings, inv-009 (I1, I3, I4, I17) and the plan's N1 approach, with one investigator dispatch (findings/A2.md). The orchestrator ran the Architecture tests to confirm I7. The 30m time box held (22:33 to about 22:50 UTC). The route runs every red first (I1, I2, I3/I4, I5, I7), then one builder dispatch, then gates that include the .NET suite.
+## Rejected alternatives
+- Open the browser only after the compile (direction b) alone: any reload, a second F5 with the tab open, or the Edge configuration still lands on the final error, and it needs a second override of Vite's lifecycle. Adding it beside (a) buys only cosmetics.
+- Go back to compiling in the config hook: it fixes F5 by bringing back I4 of inv-009, the port refusing for 60-128 s.
+- Carry I3, I4 and I6 to a later node as P2s (the lean loop's default): I1's fix rewrites the same middleware and test lines, and no later web node of bug-002 touches vite.config.ts, so carrying them would cost a second change to the same code. Kept in-node, ruled under David's delegation.
+- Re-key the loader on status 503 alone: the did-not-compile 503 must stay final (data-1.test.ts:88-95), so the compiling state needs its own marker.
+## Prior work consulted
+- docs/plans/active/inv-009.plan.md: I1, I3 (Vite opens the browser once it is listening), I4, I17, and recommendation 1 (the listen-first direction)
+- docs/plans/active/bug-002.plan.md: N1's approach, which names Docket.Web.esproj in green's file list
+- docs/plans/active/inv-005.plan.md: an earlier DATA-1 escalation (compiler field lists), unrelated cause
+- docs/lessons.md: none on trace loading
