+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"bug-002","node_id":"N1","attempt":3,"source":"reviewer","source_ref":"A2: docs/trace/bug-002/N1/verdicts/A2-reviewer.json R1, R2, R3, R4, R5; docs/trace/bug-002/N1/verdicts/A2-security.json S1 (investigation inv-010)","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"DATA-1","layer":"api","files":["src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/app/data/trace.ts","src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/app/shell/Frame.tsx","src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/app/shell/DataNotice.tsx","src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/vite.config.ts","src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/.vscode/launch.json","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/data/data-1.test.ts","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/toolchain/data-1-first-run.test.ts"],"root_cause":"UI layer: loader (app/data/trace.ts and app/shell). The schema's 'api' is the nearest allowed value. Symptom: F5 on 'API and web' opens Docket while the trail is still compiling, and the page stays on 'Could not load · trace.json could not be read (HTTP 503)' until someone reloads it by hand. CAUSE: listen-first (35122e4b) added a short-lived server state, 503 'The trail is compiling; try again in a moment.' (vite.config.ts:60-62). The only reader of /trace.json treats every non-2xx answer as final and asks only once. readJson turns any non-ok answer into '<path> could not be read (HTTP n)' and drops the body (app/data/trace.ts:245-246). loadTrace then returns state 'error' (trace.ts:264-265). useTraceFile calls loadTrace once, on mount, and never asks again (app/shell/Frame.tsx:41-53). So DataNotice draws 'Could not load' (app/shell/DataNotice.tsx:13-16). DATA-1 says 'the SPA reads only that file', and HEAD's SPA gives up on that file before it exists. TRIGGER, NOT CAUSE: Vite 8 opens the browser inside listen() (node_modules/vite/dist/node/chunks/node.js:24964). The CLI calls listen and then printUrls (node_modules/vite/dist/node/cli.js:725, :732). So holding back printUrls (vite.config.ts:49-50) holds back the 'Local:' line but not the browser, and launch.json:10 passes --open. On base the compile ran in the config hook, before listen (packet/diff.patch:9839-9844), so this window did not exist. THE HYPOTHESIS HOLDS ON ALL THREE COUNTS: Vite opens on listen, the shell does not retry a 503, and no test opens the page during the compile. The DATA-1 toolchain tests ask /trace.json with Node's fetch only (data-1-first-run.test.ts:198-227). The launch-path test removes --open (:182). Every e2e runs on build plus preview (playwright.config.ts:16), where there is no 503 window. The loader's unit tests have no 503 case (data-1.test.ts:39-109). RECURRENCE: no. This is a new fingerprint; A1/I1 was the stdout/stderr read race. The earlier route didn't prevent it because inv-009's recommendation ('let Vite listen first and answer /trace.json compiling', inv-009.plan.md:71) and N1's acceptance line 2 (bug-002.dag.yaml:28) specify only what the server answers. Yet inv-009 I3 had already recorded that Vite opens the browser once it is listening (inv-009.plan.md:39). The A1 investigation was scoped to the gate flake. FIX DIRECTIONS: (b) on its own does not remove the cause. Any page load inside the window still lands on the final error: an open tab's Vite client reloads as soon as the restarted server answers its ping (node_modules/vite/dist/client/client.mjs:1083-1088), which under listen-first is before the compile ends, as on a second F5 with the tab left open. The Edge configuration (launch.json:12-18), a manual open and a refresh do the same. (b) would also need a second override of Vite's lifecycle, like the printUrls override. (a) removes the cause on every path with the least new behaviour. While the server says it is compiling, the loader keeps the state it already has for 'trace.json is being read' (DataNotice.tsx:6-11), with no new component, and asks again until the file is ready or the compile has failed. Two constraints: the 'did not compile' 503 and the 404 must stay final after one request (data-1.test.ts:88-95), and production has no compiling state. So the re-ask must key on the compiling answer, not on status 503 alone. Today the two 503s differ only in their prose (vite.config.ts:62), as I5 notes. (c) adds (b)'s lifecycle override on top of (a) for a cosmetic gain only. Recommend (a).","fingerprint":"DATA-1|src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/app/data/trace.ts|transient-503-compiling-read-once-as-terminal-error","testable":true,"suggested_test":"First to fail on this HEAD (data-1.test.ts, unit/data). Given a fetch that answers trace.json with 503 and the body 'The trail is compiling; try again in a moment.' twice, and then serves the compiled complete fixture, When loadTrace settles, Then its state is ready with the fixture's trace, and trace.json was requested three times. On HEAD it settles as 'error' with 'trace.json could not be read (HTTP 503)' after one request. Guard in the same file: Given a 503 with 'The trail did not compile; see the console of the dev server.', Then the state is error after exactly one request. End-to-end proof, the case no test covers today: Given the dev server started on the complete trail plus 300 commits, When a Playwright page opens / before the compile ends, Then the overview draws the trail without a reload and never shows 'Could not load'.","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"DATA-1","layer":"api","files":["src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/Docket.Web.esproj","Uinsure.Policies.slnLaunch","src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/.vscode/launch.json","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Architecture.Tests/LaunchProfileTests.cs","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/toolchain/data-1-first-run.test.ts"],"root_cause":"UI layer: compiler/toolchain (the web project's launch configuration). The schema's 'api' is the nearest allowed value. Symptom: Docket.Web.esproj:4 has StartupCommand 'npx vite --port 4170 --strictPort'. It skips scripts/dev.mjs, so on a clone with no node_modules npx fetches vite from the registry, unpinned, instead of naming npm ci. WHAT VISUAL STUDIO'S F5 RUNS, FROM THE REPO: the shipped profile 'API and web' (Uinsure.Policies.slnLaunch:3-15) starts Docket.Web.esproj with DebugTarget 'Vite dev server' (:11-13). That is the node configuration at .vscode/launch.json:4-11, so F5 runs `node scripts/dev.mjs --port 4170 --strictPort --open` (launch.json:9-10), the guarded path. LaunchProfileTests.cs:69-71 records U10's D2 finding that in this profile VS 'runs Docket.Web's DebugTarget and never its StartupCommand'. The repo's only reader of the StartupCommand is LaunchProfileTests.DevServerPort, which takes the port from it (LaunchProfileTests.cs:180-186). The slnx only lists the esproj, with Build Project=false (Uinsure.Policies.slnx:48-50). So the shipped F5 never runs the StartupCommand. It can be reached only by starting Docket.Web outside that profile: on its own, or through the Edge configuration kept for Start New Instance (launch.json:12-18, LaunchProfileTests.cs:101-102). That is VS project-system behaviour the repo doesn't pin, so that last route is unconfirmed. CAUSE: N1's green (35122e4b) guarded only the launch.json program (packet/diff.patch:9762-9763) and left the StartupCommand as a second, unguarded launch command. The plan's N1 evidence names the esproj (bug-002.plan.md:23). The base comment listed 'F5, the esproj StartupCommand or npx vite' as launch paths (diff.patch:9826). data-1-trace-on-start.test.ts:4 still does. The new first-run test reads only the slnLaunch DebugTarget (data-1-first-run.test.ts:165-183). RECURRENCE: no, this is new. FIX DIRECTION: give the StartupCommand the same restore guard as the F5 target, keeping its '--port 4170' so DevServerPort still parses. Or, if it isn't a supported path, say so where it is declared. It doesn't change the F5 outcome, so P2 stands.","fingerprint":"DATA-1|src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/Docket.Web.esproj|startupcommand-npx-vite-bypasses-restore-guard","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given a fresh copy of the web project with no node_modules and npm set offline, When the esproj's StartupCommand is run exactly as written from the project folder, Then the output names npm ci and src/Uinsure.Policies.Web, with no 'Cannot find module' and no attempt to fetch vite from the registry (data-1-first-run.test.ts). On HEAD npx tries to resolve vite from the registry and never names npm ci.","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I3","rule_id":"DATA-1","layer":"api","files":["src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/vite.config.ts"],"root_cause":"UI layer: compiler/toolchain (the dev-server plugin in vite.config.ts). The schema's 'api' is the nearest allowed value. Symptom: in dev, a request with a malformed %-escape on any path, not only /trace*, gets a 500 instead of reaching Vite. Cause: vite.config.ts:53 runs decodeURIComponent on every request URL before the path filter at :54. It throws URIError on a malformed escape, and connect turns the throw into a 500. Vite's own transform middleware handles the same input by warning and calling next() (node_modules/vite/dist/node/chunks/node.js:20351-20356), so the plugin overrides Vite's policy for every path. This node introduced the decode: base read the raw path (packet/diff.patch:9874-9875). It is needed only by the traversal guard for /trace.json and /trace/* (vite.config.ts:55-56). This finding deliberately covers both R3 and the decode half of S1: same line, same cause. S1's EISDIR half has its own cause (I4). RECURRENCE: no. FIX DIRECTION: decide whether the request is for /trace.json or /trace/* before decoding, decode only for those, and answer a malformed escape there with a 4xx instead of throwing.","fingerprint":"DATA-1|src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/vite.config.ts|decodeuricomponent-before-trace-path-filter","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the dev server on the complete trail with the compile finished, When GET /src/%E0%A4%A and GET /trace/%E0%A4%A, Then neither answers 500: the first is left to Vite, which warns and passes it on, and the second answers 4xx (data-1-trace-on-start.test.ts). On HEAD both are 500.","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I4","rule_id":"API8:2023","layer":"api","files":["src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/vite.config.ts"],"root_cause":"UI layer: compiler/toolchain (the dev-server plugin in vite.config.ts). The schema's 'api' is the nearest allowed value. Symptom (S1, second half): GET /trace/ on the dev server answers 500. Cause: '/trace/' resolves to public/trace (vite.config.ts:55), which passes startsWith(publicDir + sep). existsSync is true for a directory (:56), so readFileSync throws EISDIR at :58, and connect turns that into a 500. The guard checks that the path exists, not that it is a file. Separate from I3, which is the decode; S1 named both causes in one finding. RECURRENCE: no. FIX DIRECTION: serve only regular files under public/, and answer 404 for anything else, as the code already does for a path that doesn't exist (:60).","fingerprint":"API8:2023|src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/vite.config.ts|existssync-accepts-directory-readfilesync-eisdir","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the dev server on the complete trail with the compile finished, When GET /trace/ and GET /trace/build/, Then each answers 404, not 500 (data-1-trace-on-start.test.ts). On HEAD each is 500.","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I5","rule_id":"DATA-1","layer":"tests","files":["tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/toolchain/data-1-first-run.test.ts","src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/vite.config.ts"],"root_cause":"Symptom: the 'first answer says the trail is compiling' assertion would also pass a server that answered 'did not compile' during the compile. Cause: data-1-first-run.test.ts:218 matches /compil/i, a stem shared by both 503 bodies, 'The trail is compiling…' and 'The trail did not compile…' (vite.config.ts:62). It checks neither the status nor anything that tells the two states apart. That same lack of a reliable marker (same status, same content type, prose only) is what I1's fix direction (a) has to key on, so the test and the shell's re-ask should both rest on one distinguishable compiling signal. Not merged with I1: the cause here is the test's weak expectation. RECURRENCE: no. FIX DIRECTION (tester): make the first-answer assertion name the compiling state exactly and require the 503 status. That is stricter, not weaker.","fingerprint":"DATA-1|tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/toolchain/data-1-first-run.test.ts|compil-regex-matches-both-503-bodies","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the dev server on the complete trail plus 300 commits, When the first /trace.json answer arrives, Then it is 503 and states that the trail is compiling, and it is not the 'did not compile' answer (data-1-first-run.test.ts). It passes on HEAD, and fails against a server that answers 'did not compile' while compiling, which the current /compil/i accepts.","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I6","rule_id":"DATA-1","layer":"tests","files":["tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/toolchain/data-1-trace-on-start.test.ts"],"root_cause":"Symptom: the describe title 'the dev server compiles the trail before it serves' (data-1-trace-on-start.test.ts:147) and the header's 'compiles the trail first' (:2-5) state the opposite of the behaviour at HEAD, which listens first (vite.config.ts:26-28). Cause: the green 35122e4b reversed the design, and the builder may not edit test files. The only later test commit, 9972c248 (the A1/I1 fix), was scoped to the waitFor observation, so no task owned re-stating this file's description. The header at :4 also still lists 'the StartupCommand, npx vite' as an F5 launch path (see I2). RECURRENCE: no. FIX DIRECTION (tester): re-state the describe title and the header so they say what the server does now: it listens at once, answers compiling, then serves or reports. Leave every assertion as it is.","fingerprint":"DATA-1|tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/toolchain/data-1-trace-on-start.test.ts|stale-compile-first-describe-and-header","testable":false,"suggested_test":null,"untestable_reason":"The defect is prose in a describe title and a file comment. Neither carries behaviour, and the web-testing skill says describe titles don't count toward the rule tag. No assertion can fail on it. Review against vite.config.ts:26-28 is the check."},{"id":"I7","rule_id":"DATA-1","layer":"tests","files":["tests/Uinsure.Policies.Architecture.Tests/LaunchProfileTests.cs","src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/.vscode/launch.json"],"root_cause":"Beyond the A2 verdicts, found while answering R2. Symptom, from reading: I couldn't run dotnet test here. LaunchProfileTests.API_and_web_profile_debugs_the_web_app_in_a_node_configuration_that_runs_Vite_on_the_StartupCommand_port_with_strictPort fails at HEAD. Cause: the green 35122e4b changed the DebugTarget's program to ${workspaceFolder}/scripts/dev.mjs (launch.json:9, packet/diff.patch:9762-9763). LaunchProfileTests.cs:85 still asserts that the project-relative program equals 'node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js', and ProjectRelative (:152-164) reduces HEAD's value to 'scripts/dev.mjs', so the assertion cannot pass. The gates were scoped to npm, and packet/gates.jsonl:1-11 holds no .NET test receipt. The reviewer also notes there was none ('N1 touches no .NET code'), so the break went unseen. Per CLAUDE.md, pre-push runs the full suite, so a push of this branch will be refused. The test's intent ('runs Vite itself', :70-71) still holds, because dev.mjs imports vite.js in the same process (scripts/dev.mjs:13); only the pinned path is stale. RECURRENCE: no. FIX DIRECTION (tester, an existing test's expected value tracking an intended change, shown to David as such): pin the guarded entry the DebugTarget now runs, and run the .NET Architecture.Tests as a gate for this node, since it changed a file they read.","fingerprint":"DATA-1|tests/Uinsure.Policies.Architecture.Tests/LaunchProfileTests.cs|launch-json-program-pin-not-moved-with-dev-mjs","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given HEAD's .vscode/launch.json, When dotnet test runs Uinsure.Policies.Architecture.Tests, Then the DebugTarget's program pin names the guarded entry (scripts/dev.mjs) and the test passes. On HEAD it fails at LaunchProfileTests.cs:85 with expected 'node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js', actual 'scripts/dev.mjs' (LaunchProfileTests).","untestable_reason":null}],"previous_attempts":["attempt 1 · red 6ee2e957 ok · green 35122e4b · gate.green FAIL: flaky read race between stdout and stderr (fingerprint DATA-1|tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/toolchain/data-1-trace-on-start.test.ts|stdout-stderr-read-race-snapshot-at-local)","attempt 2 · findings A1 (I1 untestable; test-observation fix 9972c248 held 393/393 three times, gates.jsonl:1) · gates ok · review A2: reviewer FAIL R1-R5, security PASS with S1 P2. No A2 cause shares A1's fingerprint; the A1 fix removed its own cause, and the A2 causes come from the listen-first design's consumer side and launch paths, which A1 never examined","attempt 3 · investigation inv-010 opened on round A2"]}
